Coded the row for Gail Griffin / data-centers as **BLANK (direction-only)**. HB2756 (2026) — which she prime-sponsored, voted for, and which was signed into law — creates ratepayer-protection cost-allocation options and demand reporting for "extra high load factor customers," but doesn't match any single rung's full clause set (no moratorium, no absolute cost-pass-through bar, no impact-assessment/community-benefit gate, no permitting provisions). File written to `labels/coder-2.json`.
